        "created_at": "2019-04-24T09:32:33Z",
        "updated_at": "2019-04-24T09:32:33Z",
        "body": "A workaround for us would be to fire off a single global task that keeps track of all open connections, and closes them on `asyncio.CancelledError`.\r\n\r\nThat wouldn't work with `loop.run_until_complete(f()) / loop.close()`, but it would work with `asyncio.run(f())`, since that correctly makes sure to cancel any outstanding tasks.",
