        "updated_at": "2019-04-24T11:07:39Z",
        "body": "Version 0.2.1 will now cleanup keep-alive connection on `ConnectionPool.close()`\r\n\r\nI still think there's a valid python bug here, but we can at least make sure to avoid this issue if we cleanup our resources properly. Suggested usages are either:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nasync with httpcore.ConnectionPool(ssl=ssl) as http:\r\n    response = await http.request('GET', 'https://httpbin.org/get')\r\n```\r\n\r\nOr:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nhttp = httpcore.ConnectionPool(ssl=ssl)\r\nresponse = await http.request('GET', 'https://httpbin.org/get')\r\nhttp.close()\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis should also play nicely with `request_async` sessions.",
